    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Design Matrix <formula id="43">$ \Phi $</formula> and the corresponding target vector <formula id="44">$ \mathrm{T} $</formula></para>
<para>An aggregation matrix composed of \phi_i matrices <verbatim>Phi = | \phi_1 |
      | \phi_2 |
      | ...    |
      | \phi_N |
</verbatim></para>
<para>where N corresponds to the number of structures in a provided <ref refid="structStructureDB" kindref="compound">StructureDB</ref>.</para>
<para>The ordering in <formula id="45">$ \phi_i $</formula> <verbatim>| energy of the 1st structure
| force on the 1st atom in the x-dir
| force on the 1st atom in the y-dir
| force on the 1st atom in the z-dir
| force on the 2st atom in the x-dir
| ...
| force on the n-th atom in the z-dir
| stress xx
| stress xy
| stress xz
| stress yy
| stress yz
| stress zz
</verbatim></para>
<para>We need to know: <ref refid="classConfig_1STRESS" kindref="member">STRESS</ref>, <ref refid="classConfig_1FORCE" kindref="member">FORCE</ref></para>
<para>Scalling factors <ref refid="classConfig_1FWEIGHT" kindref="member">FWEIGHT</ref>, <ref refid="classConfig_1SWEIGHT" kindref="member">SWEIGHT</ref></para>
<para>Default scalling:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Forces are scaled by 1/N_i/3 where N_i is a number of atoms in the i-th structure.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Stresses are scaled by 1/6.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Energies are scaled by 1/N_i</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Mode</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="structFunc__Base" kindref="compound">Func_Base</ref> child -&gt; <ref refid="structBF__Base" kindref="compound">BF_Base</ref> or <ref refid="classKern__Base" kindref="compound">Kern_Base</ref> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
